{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 his father Raymond II was the Count of Tripoli and his mother Hodierna was the daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem. \nRaymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152 after his father was murdered by the Hashshashin. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during his reign he was a strong supporter of the King of Jerusalem and participated in several military campaigns against the Muslim states. \nRaymond III was also a skilled diplomat and formed alliances with other Christian states in the region. \n*Capture and Later Life* \nRaymond III was captured by Saladin in 1164 during a battle near Panias he was imprisoned for several years before being released in 1174. \nAfter his release Raymond III continued to play a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \nRaymond III was a regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem from 1184 to 1186 during the minority of King Baldwin V. \n*Relationships and Family* \nRaymond III married Hodierna of Jerusalem but the marriage was childless. \nRaymond III had a close relationship with King Amalric I of Jerusalem who was his cousin. \nRaymond III also had a close relationship with the Byzantine Emperor Manuel I Comnenus who was his ally. \nRaymond III died in 1187 without an heir and was succeeded by his nephew Raymond of Antioch. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III was a significant figure in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. \nHe played a major role in the politics of the region and formed alliances with other Christian states. \nRaymond III was also a skilled military leader and participated in several battles against the Muslim states. \nHis legacy continued to shape the history of the region for centuries after his death. \nRaymond III was remembered as a brave and skilled leader who fought to protect the Christian states in the region. \nHis life and reign are still studied by historians today who seek to understand the complex politics of the medieval Middle East.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.00043096792069263756}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00012432756193447858}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.20712825655937195}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.710232675075531}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -5.602820692729438e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.023202933371067047}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.0009124883217737079}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "7", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.10644540935754776}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.007799291517585516}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.026432808488607407}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.025843778625130653}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.00012385078298393637}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0012978235026821494}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " H", 